# Cloudflare Pages redirects
#
# This is a multi-page static website, not a single-page app, so there is
# deliberately NO catch-all rewrite to /index.html. Cloudflare Pages serves the
# real file when it exists and serves 404.html for anything else, which keeps
# deep links such as /admin-login.html working and stops broken URLs from
# silently returning the homepage with HTTP 200.
#
# There is also no /api/* proxy to the Cloudflare Worker. Pages accepts the
# rule in this file but does not honour a proxy to an external origin - it
# returns 404. That is fine, because API traffic never goes through Pages:
#
#   js/config.js points every /api/ request straight at
#   https://csa-api.rashidjumachepkwony.workers.dev
#
# so the browser talks to the Worker cross-origin, and the Worker allows this
# site's origin via its CORS policy. The pages that do not load js/config.js
# (about, contact, parents-corner, portal, 404 and the Google verification
# file) make no API calls.
#
# If you ever need a same-origin /api path, add a route to the Worker itself
# rather than proxying from Pages.
